# Our own scratch notes — never part of the submission.
NOTES.md

# Python virtual environments — machine-specific, huge, and reproducible
# from requirements.txt / airflow/requirements-airflow.txt alone. Never
# commit these. (.venv-airflow/ is the separate venv Airflow gets — see
# "Why Airflow gets its own virtual environment" in airflow/README.md.)
.venv/
airflow/.venv-airflow/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# dlt — real (if throwaway) local credentials. example.secrets.toml is the
# committed template; this is the file it gets copied to. Lives at the repo
# root (not under ingestion/) because dlt resolves .dlt relative to the
# current working directory you RUN the script from, not the script's own
# location — and we always run it as `python ingestion/dlt_pipeline.py`
# from the repo root.
.dlt/secrets.toml

# Machine-specific Docker port remap — see the file itself for why. Never
# part of the submission; docker-compose.yml alone matches the brief.
docker-compose.override.yml

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# dbt — build artifacts and downloaded packages, both fully reproducible
# from the project files (dbt_project.yml, packages.yml) plus a fresh
# `dbt deps` / `dbt build`. profiles.yml itself isn't here because it
# isn't even in the repo — it lives at ~/.dbt/profiles.yml by dbt
# convention (see profiles.yml.example for the committed template).
nordstack_analytics/target/
nordstack_analytics/dbt_packages/
nordstack_analytics/logs/
# dbt also writes logs/ at the invocation directory, which is wherever a
# command happened to be run from (repo root or nordstack_analytics/,
# depending on habit) — ignoring it at both locations rather than
# depending on always cd-ing into the same place first.
logs/

# We'll extend this as we add each remaining piece (Airflow logs, etc.)
# rather than pre-guessing it all now.
airflow/docker/.user.yml
# dbt-generated, machine-specific telemetry ID -- never part of the submission.
